<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia private, public unions agree to strike.</title>
<headline>Colombia private, public unions agree to strike.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's main public and private sector unions agreed Friday to launch an indefinite national strike starting February 4 or February 11, union officials said.</p>
<p>The strike will involve several million unionized workers, including key oil workers, dock workers, medical staff and communications workers. The unions will meet Monday, January 20 at 5 pm (2300 GMT) to decide on which of the two dates to begin the stoppage.</p>
</text>
